import{_ as n,o as t,c as a,a2 as i}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 702 | Transcendence Orthodox Definition · Transcendence Is Not Running Away — Critique of Individual-Escape Transcendence","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 702 | Transcendence Orthodox Definition · Transcendence Is Not Running Away — Critique of Individual-Escape Transcendence","no":702,"module":4,"tags":["Transcendence","Run-Away Critique","Individual Escape","Causal Self-Discipline","Collective Ascension"],"related":["05-Myriad Ranks Advance-Together Basic Program","83-Observe-First-Then-Limitedly-Intervene Guideline","26-Individual-and-Collective Balance Principle"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0702_模块4-超脱不是逃跑.md","filePath":"en/0702_模块4-超脱不是逃跑.md"}'),o={name:"en/0702_模块4-超脱不是逃跑.md"};function r(s,e,l,c,d,u){return t(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[i('<h1 id="entry-702-transcendence-orthodox-definition-·-transcendence-is-not-running-away-—-critique-of-individual-escape-transcendence" tabindex="-1">Entry 702 | Transcendence Orthodox Definition · Transcendence Is Not Running Away — Critique of Individual-Escape Transcendence <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-702-transcendence-orthodox-definition-·-transcendence-is-not-running-away-—-critique-of-individual-escape-transcendence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 702 | Transcendence Orthodox Definition · Transcendence Is Not Running Away — Critique of Individual-Escape Transcendence&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 05, 83, 26</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-however-far-you-run-you-cannot-run-out-of-causality" tabindex="-1">Introduction: however far you run, you cannot run out of causality <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-however-far-you-run-you-cannot-run-out-of-causality" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: however far you run, you cannot run out of causality&quot;">​</a></h2><p>&quot;I have transcended the red dust, and from now on have no entanglement with the mortal world.&quot; — this sentence, in Myriad-Heavens web novels, is taken as a strong one&#39;s medal, but in Heng Yuan Zhou it is a <strong>deserter&#39;s registration form</strong>. Individual-escape transcendence is the most insidious of the three pseudo-transcendence brothers: it does not manifest as predation, nor as laziness; it wears the philosophical coat of &quot;having seen through the world,&quot; yet does the deed of dropping Myriad Ranks and running off alone.</p><p>The six top-level axioms here simultaneously judge it: the anti-predation axiom does not directly name &quot;running away,&quot; but the runner&#39;s power source is often stock accumulated by predation in early years; the republican axiom of Myriad Races asks — by what right do you alone leave, leaving Myriad Ranks who also gave and also have evolution qualification in place? The collective-ascension axiom most directly sentences it to death: the strong do not ascend alone. The causal self-discipline axiom adds the last blade: you think severing bonds severs causality? Causality does not vanish by your will; it is only thrown behind you, continuing to ferment in a more twisted way. The law-first axiom ensures the law definition that &quot;running away is not transcendence&quot; stays stable, not loosened by some web-novel protagonist&#39;s tragic ending.</p><p>Universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing/layabouts retain a floor basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose more higher-level infinity. Everyone inherently possesses infinite origin, so predation naturally loses meaning.</p><h2 id="i-individual-escape-transcendence-s-three-typical-scripts" tabindex="-1">I: Individual-Escape Transcendence&#39;s Three Typical Scripts <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-individual-escape-transcendence-s-three-typical-scripts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I: Individual-Escape Transcendence&#39;s Three Typical Scripts&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Dissecting the long web-novel river, individual-escape transcendence has three recurring scripts:</p><ol><li><strong>Tribulation-in-the-mortal-world type</strong>: the protagonist goes through life and death, relatives and friends die out, heart cold, &quot;sees through the red dust,&quot; shatters the sky with one palm and leaves, leaving a devastated civilization to clean up the wreckage itself;</li><li><strong>Plane-ascension type</strong>: the protagonist breaks through everything in the mortal realm, ascends to the upper realm, and the mortal realm from then on has nothing to do with him; breaks through again in the upper realm, ascends higher, dropping civilizations behind all the way;</li><li><strong>Autocratic-for-eons type</strong>: the protagonist, to protect something, seals all enemies and all possibilities, alone guarding the end of the river of time, forbidding any later person to approach.</li></ol><p>The three scripts look solemn, but are essentially the same: <strong>packaging &quot;I&#39;m leaving&quot; as &quot;I&#39;ve transcended,&quot; packaging &quot;I&#39;ve dropped Myriad Ranks&quot; as &quot;Myriad Ranks no longer need me.&quot;</strong></p><h2 id="ii-why-running-away-is-not-transcendence-three-books-of-causal-debts" tabindex="-1">II: Why Running Away Is Not Transcendence: Three Books of Causal Debts <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-running-away-is-not-transcendence-three-books-of-causal-debts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II: Why Running Away Is Not Transcendence: Three Books of Causal Debts&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou does not recognize running-away transcendence not by moralizing, but by accounting. Under the causal self-discipline axiom, the runner owes three books of debts never repayable:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Account</th><th>Content</th><th>Consequence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Human-debt account</td><td>The causality mentors, fellow disciples, and clansmen gave on the cultivation road</td><td>All cut off, and you snap one ring in the Myriad-Rank origin cycle</td></tr><tr><td>Law account</td><td>Your plane was stable because of your presence; once you leave, the law anchor destabilizes</td><td>Local law drifts, and civilizational-regression risk rises exponentially</td></tr><tr><td>Example account</td><td>Countless later people take you as their model, learning &quot;can&#39;t beat it so run, ascend and forget the root&quot;</td><td>The whole civilization&#39;s strong-one ethics collapse, and the predation faction slips in</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Most critical is the third account. In the Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision&#39;s records, a strong one&#39;s &quot;running away&quot; is not a private choice, but a public event — it is seen by all beings network-wide, imitated by later people, interpreted by the predation faction as &quot;the strong should do it this way.&quot; This is why the causal self-discipline axiom requires cross-plane operations strictly reported: you may not be unable to leave, you may not leave <strong>without saying hello, without handover, without an anchor</strong>.</p><h2 id="iii-the-essential-difference-from-going-far-to-cultivate" tabindex="-1">III: The Essential Difference from &quot;Going Far to Cultivate&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-the-essential-difference-from-going-far-to-cultivate" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III: The Essential Difference from &quot;Going Far to Cultivate&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Some will argue: doesn&#39;t Heng Yuan Zhou also do cross-plane exploration, also open new universes (see Post 719)? What&#39;s the difference between going far to cultivate and running-away transcendence?</p><p>There are three differences, each a hard standard:</p><ol><li><strong>Whether an anchor is left</strong>: the far-going cultivator must leave a law anchor and successor in the original plane, maintaining law stability; the runner snaps everything at once;</li><li><strong>Whether causality is reported</strong>: the far-going cultivator reports the journey per observe-first-then-limitedly-intervene, completing handover before leaving; the runner disappears soundlessly;</li><li><strong>Whether the feedback loop is kept</strong>: the far-going cultivator brings back knowledge, law-weaving experience, and incremental resources from new planes, feeding back to Myriad Ranks via the Selfless Dao; the runner only takes power, leaving not a thread.</li></ol><p>All three present is called &quot;opening up&quot;; all three absent is called &quot;running away.&quot; Heng Yuan Zhou does not oppose strong ones going far; Heng Yuan Zhou opposes <strong>going far then cutting the loop back to the Myriad-Rank origin two-way cycle</strong>.</p><h2 id="iv-lin-hao-type-counter-example-writing-running-away-as-responsibility" tabindex="-1">IV: Lin Hao-Type Counter-Example: Writing &quot;Running Away&quot; as &quot;Responsibility&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-lin-hao-type-counter-example-writing-running-away-as-responsibility" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV: Lin Hao-Type Counter-Example: Writing &quot;Running Away&quot; as &quot;Responsibility&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>In the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s narrative paradigm, protagonist Lin Hao&#39;s growth path is precisely the opposite of running-away transcendence: every realm breakthrough, he does not fly up one step then let go, but turns back to bring along fellow-realm latecomers. His &quot;transcendence&quot; is not flying to some higher unoccupied realm, but in the post of the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm, weaving the Myriad-Rank origin two-way cycle&#39;s loop tighter — activating one more plane, covering one more clan, opening one more method, and civilizational weight grows by one more point.</p><p>This is not moral loftiness, but law requirement. Per the plane-sovereign strong-one four-dimensional assessment, the responsibility dimension is 15% and heart-nature 25%; a runner&#39;s heart-nature score is pierced at the ethical-review stage: deep consciousness scanning reads out the &quot;drop Myriad Ranks and ascend alone&quot; subconscious, situational stress testing replays the choice of &quot;you leave and the civilization behind collapses,&quot; and if he chooses &quot;leave,&quot; he does not pass.</p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V: Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V: Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: the runner takes away lifetime cultivation&#39;s entire compute and law-weaving ability into ownerless land, a thorough waste of civilization increment</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: if the runner accumulated by predation in early years, his stock was unclean to begin with; running away does not repay, only makes the creditor unable to find him</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo protagonists ascend and cut contact, with the mortal realm locked in the fierce realm with no further improvement; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s transcendent ones before leaving must leave an anchor, a successor, and a knowledge loop</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: running-away transcendence leaves 99% of Myriad Ranks in place to fend for themselves, directly violating the Myriad-Rank 99% full-coverage promise</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the runner&#39;s methods and experience disappear with him, hyper-multiverse-tier knowledge is privately taken, openness goes to zero</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinity</strong>: the universal equal infinite law — within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization everyone inherently possesses basic infinite power; the easygoing layabouts retain a floor basic infinity and are not eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose higher-level infinity; everyone inherently possesses infinite origin, and predation naturally loses meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Transcendence is not a &quot;I&#39;m leaving.&quot; You may go to the farthest plane, to the newest universe, to law&#39;s wildest frontier — but as long as you are still doing work in the Myriad-Rank origin two-way cycle, as long as you still keep the anchor, the successor, and the Selfless Dao loop, however far you go you are a transcendent one. Once you cut these three loops, however far you go you are only a deserter. <strong>Running away is not transcendence; running away only drags the debt owed Myriad Ranks from today to tomorrow.</strong></p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/05-万族共进基本纲领.html">Entry 05 · Myriad Ranks Advance-Together Basic Program</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/83-先观测后有限干涉准则.html">Entry 83 · Observe-First-Then-Limitedly-Intervene Guideline</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/26-个体与集体平衡原理.html">Entry 26 · Individual-and-Collective Balance Principle</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/28-跨位面锚点连接.html">Entry 28 · Cross-Plane Anchor Connection</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',28)])])}const p=n(o,[["render",r]]);export{g as __pageData,p as default};
